main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ member alias template two-parallel-pack expansion: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.variadic]/4-5 + [temp.alias]/2.  A MEMBER alias template
whose body expands two parallel packs (its own pack + the enclosing class's
pack) -- the shape of libstdc++'s std::tuple _TupleConstraints
(__constructible/__convertible = __and_<is_X<_Types, _UTypes>...>) -- does not
fold to the correct constant when instantiated with a concrete pack: g++/clang++
compute chk() == 3, but CBMC leaves the result non-constant (unconstrained).
This is the root cause of cpp17_tuple_basic (std::make_tuple's forwarding
constructor is SFINAE-rejected because the constraint is not a constant true).
It is DISTINCT from the now-fixed single-pack non-type-argument bug
(cpp11_nontype_pack_member_value_args), which was a hard "found no match for
symbol 'value'" on the 2nd non-type pack argument.  Arguments are deduced to
avoid the separate parser bug (cpp11_qualified_nested_template_id_no_keyword).
Flip to CORE once a two-parallel-pack member-alias body folds to the correct
constant.
